      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Swelling, warmth, and redness in your calf could be a sign of a serious condition, like deep vein thrombosis. I strongly advise against self-treatment. However, to reduce swelling, you can elevate your leg above heart level, apply a cold pack for 20 minutes at a time, and take over-the-counter anti-inflammatory medication like ibuprofen, but only if you're not allergic or have any contraindications. If symptoms persist or worsen, seek immediate medical attention. Remember, I'm here to help, but I'm not a substitute for professional medical advice.",
